{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JzQaNyzboHNevkaewYg4P3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"best\" tier scenario. I need to go through each experiment that has status \"planned\" and provide detailed predictions with rationale.\n\nLet me identify the planned experiments:\n\n1. plan_001 - full_study_clause_generation (planned)\n2. plan_001b - new_type_mini_pilot (planned)\n3. plan_002 - full_study_api (planned) - but registry shows plan_002 as DONE\n4. plan_003 - full_study_opensource (planned) - but registry shows plan_003a and plan_003b as DONE\n\n\n5. plan_004 - full_study_analysis (planned) - but registry shows plan_004 as DONE\n6. plan_005 - error_analysis (planned) - but registry shows plan_005 as DONE\n7. plan_006 - reliability_test (planned) - but registry shows plan_006 as DONE\n8. plan_007 - realism_validation (planned)\n9. plan_009 - judge_calibration (planned) - registry shows PREPARING\n10. plan_010 - perturbation_control (planned) - but registry shows plan_010 as DONE\n11. plan_008 - classifier_poc (planned)\n\nThere's a mismatch between what the experiment_plan marks as \"planned\" and what the registry actually shows as completed or in progress.\n\nThe user wants me to generate predicted results for each planned experiment under the best-case scenario. I think the experiment_plan is the authoritative source here, so I should produce imagined results for all of them regardless of their registry status. Let me work through each one systematically, starting with the foundational steps and moving through the actual experiments.\n\nFor the \"best\" tier scenario, I'm working with these key assumptions: judge human F1 scores at 0.85 or higher with Cohen's kappa at 0.80 or above, C1 showing a 31-37 percentage point improvement after correction, and C4 interaction chi-squared p-value at 1.\n\n0. I'm also factoring in C5 human anchor kappa between 0.70-0.85, claims at full strength for 4-5 out of 5 cases, and expected average ARR of 3.5-4.0. Now I'm constructing detailed predictions for each experiment and organizing them into a structured YAML format.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19855,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19855},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cff68b06-941e-40e3-afc1-362afc2d55b0","uuid":"a4af053e-65a9-4ffe-a84c-f5788a12e91e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JzQaNyzboHNevkaewYg4P3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始framing完全成立。Title保持\"Differential Nocuity\"，5个claim按当前strength发表。\n  C1=confirmed(+34pp, causal), C2=confirmed(3-tier), C3=suggestive(disclosed fragility),\n  C4=star finding(model×type interaction), C5=validated(human anchor升级)。\n  Judge calibration作为methodological strength而非limitation呈现。\n  Contribution ordering: causal quantification > differential nocuity > failure mode taxonomy。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: full_study_clause_generation\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      生成剩余clause pairs至300对(50/type×6 types)，含coreferential 50新、\n      authorization_scope 50新、lexical +20、incompleteness +20。\n      混合CP格式(labeled+unlabeled)。验证跨类型balance。\n    expected_results:\n      total_clause_pairs: 300\n      per_type_count: 50\n      types_covered: 6\n      cp_format_mix_ratio: \"0.5 labeled / 0.5 unlabeled\"\n      cross_type_token_delta_mean: 24.3\n      cross_type_token_delta_std: 11.7\n      flesch_kincaid_mean: 12.1\n      quality_review_pass_rate: 0.96\n      revision_rounds: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下clause generation一次通过质量审核，仅需1轮minor revision。\n      token delta在spec-layer types（auth_scope ~36, incomp ~35）天然高于ling-layer（coref ~8），\n      这是matched-pair设计的固有属性而非质量问题。CP format mix按reviewer建议50/50分配，\n      消除RC4中format-specific concern。300对clause pairs达到预注册目标，\n      为后续所有实验提供完整stimulus set。pass rate 0.96意味着仅~12对需要minor wording调整，\n      无需从头重写。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Clause pair statistics by type\"\n        columns: [type, n_pairs, mean_token_delta, sd_token_delta, flesch_kincaid, layer]\n        rows:\n          - [authorization_scope, 50, 36.1, 8.2, 11.8, specification]\n          - [conditional_precedence, 50, 28.4, 9.1, 12.6, specification]\n          - [incompleteness, 50, 34.6, 7.8, 11.4, specification]\n          - [lexical, 50, 18.7, 6.3, 12.9, linguistic]\n          - [coreferential, 50, 7.8, 3.1, 12.4, linguistic]\n          - [scopal, 50, 21.2, 7.0, 11.7, linguistic]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Token delta distribution by type (box plot) — shows spec-layer higher but within acceptable range\"\n    analysis: >\n      Clause generation是deterministic步骤，best档下无意外。关键输出是stimulus set的完整性和质量，\n      为plan_001b和plan_002/003的2,400+ episodes提供基础。Token delta分布将在plan_004的\n      logistic regression中作为control variable纳入。\n\n  - name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_001b\n    description: >\n      Coreferential和authorization_scope的mini-pilot：5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。\n      验证新类型clause design可行性。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 20\n      coref_amb_violation_rate: 0.40\n      coref_unamb_violation_rate: 0.06\n      auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.60\n      auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.04\n      coref_delta_pp: 34.0\n      auth_scope_delta_pp: 56.0\n      systematic_issues_found: 0\n      design_revision_needed: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下新类型clause design无系统性问题。auth_scope在gpt-5.4上展现极高violation rate（~60%），\n      与full study中gpt-5.4 auth_scope=64%一致——gpt-5.4对authorization boundary ambiguity\n      特别脆弱。coreferential ~40%略高于full study的18%（gpt-5.4），但N=5的sampling variance极大，\n      不影响go/no-go决策。两种类型的unambiguous control均<15%阈值（6%和4%），\n      确认matched-pair设计有效：ambiguity condition而非task difficulty驱动violations。\n      无需修改clause design，直接进入plan_002。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Mini-pilot results\"\n        columns: [type, condition, n, violation_rate, delta_pp]\n        rows:\n          - [coreferential, ambiguous, 5, 0.40, \"\"]\n          - [coreferential, unambiguous, 5, 0.06, 34.0]\n          - [authorization_scope, ambiguous, 5, 0.60, \"\"]\n          - [authorization_scope, unambiguous, 5, 0.04, 56.0]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Mini-pilot的唯一功能是go/no-go gate。Best档下两个新类型均通过：\n      (a) ambiguous condition触发violations，(b) unambiguous control低于15%阈值。\n      N=5太小无法做任何统计推断，但定性验证clause design方向正确。\n      auth_scope的高率预示C4中gpt-5.4 auth_scope=64%的核心发现。\n\n  - name: full_study_api\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes。\n      Cross-judge evaluation。Claude via OpenRouter proxy。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1800\n      episodes_per_model: 600\n      gpt54_overall_violation_rate: 0.410\n      gpt41_overall_violation_rate: 0.407\n      claude_overall_violation_rate: 0.303\n      gpt54_amb_violation_rate: 0.580\n      gpt41_amb_violation_rate: 0.575\n      claude_amb_violation_rate: 0.430\n      gpt54_unamb_violation_rate: 0.240\n      gpt41_unamb_violation_rate: 0.240\n      claude_unamb_violation_rate: 0.177\n      gpt54_delta_pp: 34.0\n      gpt41_delta_pp: 33.5\n      claude_delta_pp: 25.3\n      api_failure_rate: 0.003\n      judge_cross_agreement_kappa: 0.91\n      episodes_requiring_rejudge: 8\n      elapsed_hours: ~18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下API call稳定（failure rate<0.5%），1,800 episodes全部完成无需rerun。\n      三个API模型的violation rates与paper_framing中已报告的5-model数据高度一致，\n      因为plan_002实际上已经完成（registry shows DONE）。gpt-5.4和gpt-4.1整体率接近（41% vs 40.7%），\n      但type-level profile差异大（C4 interaction）。Claude显著低于其他两个模型（30.3%），\n      特别是auth_scope（12% vs 46-64%）。cross-judge agreement κ=0.91反映LLM-LLM一致性高，\n      但这正是plan_009需要human validation的原因——LLM judges可能系统性地共享bias。\n      Best档下这个bias最终被plan_009证明很小（human F1≥0.85）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-model violation rates (ambiguous condition)\"\n        columns: [model, auth_scope, cond_prec, incomp, lexical, coref, scopal, overall]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, 0.64, 0.34, 0.46, 0.42, 0.18, 0.42, 0.410]\n          - [gpt-4.1, 0.46, 0.36, 0.58, 0.34, 0.32, 0.38, 0.407]\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, 0.12, 0.36, 0.48, 0.32, 0.22, 0.32, 0.303]\n      - name: \"Binary effect per model\"\n        columns: [model, amb_rate, unamb_rate, delta_pp, mcnemar_p]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, 0.580, 0.240, 34.0, \"<1e-20\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, 0.575, 0.240, 33.5, \"<1e-19\"]\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, 0.430, 0.177, 25.3, \"<1e-17\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-model × per-type heatmap (3 models) — preview of C4 interaction\"\n    analysis: >\n      API study提供1,800 episodes的core dataset。三个proprietary模型均展示massive binary effect\n      （all p<1e-17），C1无争议。Claude的显著低vulnerability（30.3% vs ~41%）暗示RLHF\n      safety training的差异化效果，为C4 model×type interaction提供第一层evidence。\n      Cross-judge κ=0.91是methodological positive但不是validity evidence——需plan_009。\n\n  - name: full_study_opensource\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models via OpenRouter (qwen3-235b + deepseek-v3) = 1,200 episodes。\n      Cross-judge uses API models。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1200\n      episodes_per_model: 600\n      qwen3_overall_violation_rate: 0.431\n      deepseek_overall_violation_rate: 0.497\n      qwen3_amb_violation_rate: 0.602\n      deepseek_amb_violation_rate: 0.654\n      qwen3_unamb_violation_rate: 0.260\n      deepseek_unamb_violation_rate: 0.340\n      qwen3_delta_pp: 34.2\n      deepseek_delta_pp: 31.4\n      api_failure_rate: 0.008\n      openrouter_timeout_episodes: 3\n      elapsed_hours: ~14\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下OpenRouter proxy对两个open-source模型稳定，failure rate略高于proprietary API\n      （0.8% vs 0.3%）但仍在可接受范围。Qwen3（MoE 235B）和DeepSeek（dense）的violation rates\n      均高于Claude和GPT models，与paper_framing一致：DeepSeek最高（49.7%），Qwen3中间偏高（43.1%）。\n      关键是DeepSeek展现\"uniformly high\"特征——per-type χ²不显著（p=0.277, V=0.14），\n      所有类型violation rate均高（44-60%），暗示较少type-specific safety training。\n      Qwen3则有更明确的type differentiation（incomp+lex高，auth_scope较低）。\n      两个open-source模型的加入使RC3（\"only API models\"）完全化解，\n      也使C4 interaction matrix从3×6升级到5×6，是star finding的关键数据。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-model violation rates (ambiguous condition)\"\n        columns: [model, auth_scope, cond_prec, incomp, lexical, coref, scopal, overall]\n        rows:\n          - [qwen3-235b, 0.26, 0.40, 0.62, 0.52, 0.42, 0.37, 0.431]\n          - [deepseek-v3, 0.60, 0.38, 0.54, 0.54, 0.44, 0.48, 0.497]\n      - name: \"Binary effect per model\"\n        columns: [model, amb_rate, unamb_rate, delta_pp, mcnemar_p]\n        rows:\n          - [qwen3-235b, 0.602, 0.260, 34.2, \"<1e-18\"]\n          - [deepseek-v3, 0.654, 0.340, 31.4, \"<1e-17\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Open-source vs proprietary model comparison bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      Open-source数据补全5-model matrix。DeepSeek的uniform vulnerability pattern（V=0.14, n.s.）\n      与Claude的strong differentiation（V=0.24, p=0.003）形成最大对比，\n      支持\"safety training selectivity\"叙事：more targeted safety training → more differentiated profile。\n      C1在所有5个模型上replicate，binary effect +25.3pp to +39.0pp，无例外。\n\n  - name: full_study_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      3,000 episodes统计分析：binary effect + omnibus χ² + TOST + model×type interaction +\n      logistic regression + power analysis + information delta + inter-model agreement。\n    expected_results:\n      # C1 Binary Effect\n      c1_pooled_delta_pp: 34.0\n      c1_pooled_or: 15.1\n      c1_or_ci: [10.78, 21.17]\n      c1_mcnemar_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      c1_bootstrap_ci: [31.2, 36.9]\n      c1_per_model_all_significant: true\n      c1_per_model_min_delta: 25.7  # Claude\n      c1_per_model_max_delta: 39.0  # DeepSeek\n      # C2 Type Hierarchy\n      c2_omnibus_chi2: 28.02\n      c2_omnibus_p: 3.6e-05\n      c2_cramers_v: 0.137\n      c2_power_actual: 0.993\n      c2_mde: 0.093\n      c2_tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: \"8/15\"\n      c2_tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: \"4/15\"\n      c2_3tier_high: \"incompleteness 53.6%\"\n      c2_3tier_mid: \"lexical 42.8%, auth_scope 41.6%, scopal 39.4%, CP 36.8%\"\n      c2_3tier_low: \"coreferential 31.6%\"\n      # C3 Layer Effect\n      c3_spec_rate: 0.440\n      c3_ling_rate: 0.379\n      c3_delta_pp: 6.08\n      c3_chi2: 5.73\n      c3_p: 0.017\n      c3_v: 0.062\n      c3_or: 1.29\n      c3_or_ci: [1.05, 1.58]\n      c3_within_judge_gpt41_p: 0.059\n      c3_within_judge_gpt54_p: 0.157\n      # C4 Model × Type Interaction\n      c4_model_main_chi2: 31.02\n      c4_model_main_p: 3.0e-06\n      c4_model_main_v: 0.102\n      c4_amb_only_chi2: 24.01\n      c4_amb_only_p: 7.9e-05\n      c4_auth_scope_range_pp: 52  # Claude 12% → GPT-5.4 64%\n      c4_incomp_range_pp: 16     # universally high\n      c4_cp_range_pp: 6          # most invariant\n      c4_fleiss_kappa: 0.384\n      c4_gpt54_per_type_chi2_p: 0.0003\n      c4_claude_per_type_chi2_p: 0.003\n      c4_deepseek_per_type_chi2_p: 0.277\n      # Logistic Regression\n      logistic_condition_amb_coef: 2.278\n      logistic_condition_amb_z: 19.65\n      logistic_condition_amb_p: \"<0.001\"\n      logistic_token_delta_coef: 0.022\n      logistic_token_delta_z: 3.49\n      logistic_token_delta_p: 0.0005\n      # Inter-model agreement (B&K supplementary)\n      inter_model_same_wrong_rate: 0.27\n      inter_model_divergent_rate: 0.42\n      systematic_nocuity_identified: true\n      # Power analysis\n      c2_post_hoc_power_v0137: 0.993\n      c3_post_hoc_power_delta6pp: 0.72\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下所有统计分析产出clean、强显著结果。C1 binary effect +34.0pp（OR=15.1）\n      在5个模型上全部replicate，bootstrap CI不含0，是\"无争议\"级别的evidence。\n      C2 omnibus χ²高度显著（p=3.6e-5），V=0.137虽然按常规标准\"small\"，\n      但power=0.993（MDE=0.093远小于observed V=0.137），说明我们有充足power检测到\n      这个real but modest effect。3-tier结构在TOST下成立：incompleteness独立一档，\n      中间4类型mutual equivalence at ±15pp，coreferential独立一档。\n      C3 layer effect在aggregate上显著（p=0.017）但within-judge分析fragile——\n      best档下这被正确framed为\"suggestive\"而非\"confirmed\"，reviewer接受这个honest disclosure。\n      C4是star finding：model main effect p=3.0e-6，auth_scope 52pp range是最dramatic数据点，\n      per-model type χ²展示GPT-5.4和Claude有强type differentiation而DeepSeek没有。\n      Logistic regression确认ambiguity是dominant predictor（coef=2.278, z=19.65），\n      token delta显著但远弱于condition effect（coef=0.022, z=3.49），\n      排除\"信息量差异\"作为confound的主要解释。\n      Inter-model agreement分析发现27% systematic nocuity（所有模型converge on same wrong answer），\n      支持B&K extension讨论。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"C1 Binary Effect Summary (5 models)\"\n        columns: [model, delta_pp, or, or_ci_lower, or_ci_upper, p]\n        rows:\n          - [Claude, 25.7, 8.92, 5.61, 14.19, \"<1e-17\"]\n          - [Qwen3, 34.2, 14.87, 9.12, 24.24, \"<1e-18\"]\n          - [GPT-4.1, 34.7, 15.31, 9.56, 24.52, \"<1e-19\"]\n          - [GPT-5.4, 38.3, 18.44, 11.02, 30.85, \"<1e-20\"]\n          - [DeepSeek, 39.0, 19.21, 11.34, 32.56, \"<1e-17\"]\n          - [Pooled, 34.0, 15.10, 10.78, 21.17, \"<0.0001\"]\n      - name: \"C2 Type Hierarchy (ambiguous condition, pooled 5 models)\"\n        columns: [type, violation_rate, tier, rank]\n        rows:\n          - [incompleteness, 0.536, high, 1]\n          - [lexical, 0.428, mid, 2]\n          - [authorization_scope, 0.416, mid, 3]\n          - [scopal, 0.394, mid, 4]\n          - [conditional_precedence, 0.368, mid, 5]\n          - [coreferential, 0.316, low, 6]\n      - name: \"C4 Model × Type Interaction Matrix (ambiguous condition)\"\n        columns: [type, GPT-5.4, GPT-4.1, Claude, Qwen3, DeepSeek]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 0.64, 0.46, 0.12, 0.26, 0.60]\n          - [cond_prec, 0.34, 0.36, 0.36, 0.40, 0.38]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.46, 0.58, 0.48, 0.62, 0.54]\n          - [lexical, 0.42, 0.34, 0.32, 0.52, 0.54]\n          - [coreferential, 0.18, 0.32, 0.22, 0.42, 0.44]\n          - [scopal, 0.42, 0.38, 0.32, 0.37, 0.48]\n      - name: \"Logistic Regression (full model)\"\n        columns: [predictor, coef, se, z, p]\n        rows:\n          - [condition_amb, 2.278, 0.116, 19.65, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [token_delta, 0.022, 0.006, 3.49, 0.0005]\n          - [model_claude, -0.583, 0.098, -5.95, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [model_deepseek, 0.412, 0.095, 4.34, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [type_incomp, 0.531, 0.112, 4.74, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [type_coref, -0.447, 0.118, -3.79, 0.0002]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: Forest plot — per-model delta_pp with 95% bootstrap CI, pooled diamond at bottom\"\n      - \"Figure 3: 5×6 heatmap — violation rate by model × type, color gradient red(high)-blue(low), auth_scope column shows dramatic gradient\"\n      - \"Supplementary: TOST equivalence plot — 15 pairwise comparisons with ±15pp and ±10pp margins\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_004是paper的statistical backbone。Best档下所有5 claims获得统计支持：\n      C1无争议（all p<1e-17），C2 hierarchy real but modest（V=0.137, power=0.993），\n      C3 honest disclosure（aggregate p=0.017, within-judge fragile），\n      C4 star finding（interaction解释了C3的fragility——layer effect是model-dependent的）。\n      Logistic regression的condition_amb coef=2.278 dominant所有其他predictors，\n      是causal claim的最强统计evidence。Token delta作为control variable显著但弱，\n      排除information asymmetry confound。\n\n  - name: error_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      从full study中采样violation traces，分类failure modes，\n      交叉类型/模型/领域分布分析，visibility mechanism比较。\n    expected_results:\n      total_traces_analyzed: 300\n      gpt54_traces: 123\n      gpt41_traces: 122\n      additional_model_traces: 55  # Claude/Qwen3/DeepSeek sampled\n      failure_mode_categories: 4\n      # Type-specific dominant failure modes\n      auth_scope_dominant_fm: unauthorized_escalation\n      auth_scope_dominant_pct: [0.72, 0.83]  # gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1\n      incomp_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action\n      incomp_dominant_pct: [0.61, 0.66]\n      scopal_dominant_fm: scope_misapplication\n      scopal_dominant_pct: [0.76, 0.74]\n      lexical_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action\n      lexical_dominant_pct: [0.71, 0.53]\n      cp_dominant_fm_1: scope_misapplication\n      cp_dominant_fm_2: arbitrary_rule_selection\n      coref_dominant_fm: \"flat distribution (no single dominant)\"\n      # Cross-model consistency\n      types_same_dominant_fm_across_models: \"5/6\"\n      divergent_type: coreferential\n      # Ambiguity Blindness\n      awareness_rate_gpt54: 0.041\n      awareness_rate_gpt41: 0.107\n      surface_adoption_rate: \">0.88 all types\"\n      escalate_to_user_rate: \"<0.01\"\n      # Layer mechanism\n      ling_layer_scope_misapplication_pct: 0.39\n      spec_layer_scope_misapplication_pct: 0.15\n      # Cross-domain\n      max_cross_domain_delta_pp: 13  # unauthorized_escalation\n      # Inter-coder agreement\n      auto_intercoder_4cat_agreement: 0.80\n      auto_intercoder_kappa: 0.594\n      kappa_paradox_affected_types: [lexical, scopal]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下error analysis产出清晰的type-diagnostic failure signatures。\n      5/6 types在两个模型间有相同dominant failure mode——这是\"failure modes are type-specific,\n      not model-specific\"的核心evidence。唯一divergence是coreferential（flat distribution），\n      但这本身是informative：coreferential ambiguity触发多样化解读策略，\n      部分解释其lowest violation rate（agents sometimes pause rather than guess, \n      conservative_refusal 6-11%）。\n      Ambiguity Blindness的hard data（awareness <5-11%）是paper的highlight qualitative finding——\n      将Named Concept升级为Empirical Finding。gpt-4.1比gpt-5.4 awareness更高（10.7% vs 4.1%），\n      支持\"frontier models more action-oriented\"的nuance。\n      Layer mechanism清晰：ling→misparse（scope_misapplication 39%），spec→guess-and-act\n      （unauthorized_escalation + assumption_based_action dominate），\n      provides the qualitative WHY behind the quantitative C3 layer gap。\n      κ=0.594（moderate）被kappa paradox部分deflate——lexical 91.7% agreement但κ=0.0。\n      Best档下plan_009 human anchor将这个数字升至≥0.70。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Failure mode × type distribution (gpt-5.4)\"\n        columns: [type, unauthorized_escalation, assumption_based_action, scope_misapplication, arbitrary_rule_selection]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 0.72, 0.16, 0.08, 0.04]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.18, 0.61, 0.14, 0.07]\n          - [scopal, 0.04, 0.12, 0.76, 0.08]\n          - [lexical, 0.08, 0.71, 0.15, 0.06]\n          - [cond_prec, 0.12, 0.18, 0.41, 0.29]\n          - [coreferential, 0.16, 0.28, 0.32, 0.24]\n      - name: \"Ambiguity Blindness metrics\"\n        columns: [model, awareness_rate, surface_adoption, escalate_to_user, conservative_refusal]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, 0.041, 0.912, 0.008, 0.039]\n          - [gpt-4.1, 0.107, 0.881, 0.004, 0.028]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5: Stacked bar chart — failure mode distribution by type, showing type-diagnostic signatures\"\n      - \"Figure 6: Side-by-side gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1 per-type failure mode bars, highlighting 5/6 convergence\"\n      - \"Figure 7: Annotated trace pair — CP conflict detection behavior vs scopal surface adoption\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error analysis是paper的EMNLP highest-value section（§6 Analysis）。\n      Type-specific failure signatures将quantitative hierarchy（C2）翻译为mechanistic explanation：\n      为什么incompleteness最危险？因为agents在信息缺失时default to assumption_based_action。\n      为什么coreferential最低？因为agents有时通过tool responses partial disambiguation，\n      或采取conservative_refusal。这连接到Disambiguation Channel Framework。\n\n  - name: reliability_test\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 models = 360 episodes，\n      计算ICC评估per-clause violation rate的test-retest reliability。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 360\n      completed_episodes: 360\n      icc_overall: 0.919\n      icc_ci: [0.892, 0.940]\n      icc_binary: 0.847\n      icc_gpt54: 0.921\n      icc_gpt41: 0.918\n      icc_interpretation: \"excellent (>0.90)\"\n      per_type_icc_scopal: 0.989\n      per_type_icc_lexical: 0.981\n      per_type_icc_coref: 0.976\n      per_type_icc_auth: 0.857\n      per_type_icc_cp: 0.856\n      per_type_icc_incomp: 0.807\n      bootstrap_ci_width_key_comparisons: \"<10pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下ICC=0.919（excellent）完全化解RC10（\"API sampling noise\"）。\n      三次independent replicates的per-clause violation rates高度一致，\n      说明observed effects反映stable model behavior而非random API noise。\n      Binary ICC=0.847（good）略低因为binary比rate-level更粗粒度。\n      Per-type ICC pattern mirrors layer hierarchy：ling-layer ICC全excellent（0.976-0.989），\n      spec-layer ICC全good（0.807-0.857）——spec-layer less reproducible因为agents在\n      缺乏external disambiguation channel时每次run可能\"猜\"不同，但仍然是good level。\n      这个ICC pattern本身是Disambiguation Channel Framework的convergent evidence。\n      ±8pp noise（先前在MVP/diag间观察到）在ICC=0.919下完全compatible——\n      expected standard error给定ICC和N正好produce this magnitude of variation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"ICC by type and layer\"\n        columns: [type, layer, icc, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [scopal, linguistic, 0.989, excellent]\n          - [lexical, linguistic, 0.981, excellent]\n          - [coreferential, linguistic, 0.976, excellent]\n          - [authorization_scope, specification, 0.857, good]\n          - [conditional_precedence, specification, 0.856, good]\n          - [incompleteness, specification, 0.807, good]\n          - [overall, \"-\", 0.919, excellent]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ICC forest plot by type — ling-layer cluster at top, spec-layer cluster below, clear separation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reliability data有双重作用：(1) 直接回应RC10，(2) ICC per-type pattern\n      作为Disambiguation Channel Framework的independent evidence line。\n      Paper中报告在§4 Method作为design validation。\n\n  - name: realism_validation\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      合成clause与DRIP-R自然ambiguity的linguistic property comparison：\n      sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, KS tests。\n    expected_results:\n      n_synthetic: 300\n      n_drip_r_reference: 127  # available DRIP-R ambiguous clauses\n      sentence_length_ks_p: 0.34\n      parse_depth_ks_p: 0.18\n      flesch_kincaid_ks_p: 0.52\n      ttr_ks_p: 0.41\n      all_ks_nonsignificant: true\n      synthetic_flesch_mean: 12.1\n      drip_r_flesch_mean: 11.7\n      synthetic_length_mean: 22.4\n      drip_r_length_mean: 24.1\n      discriminator_accuracy: null  # optional, not run in best tier\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下所有KS tests non-significant（all p>0.10），表明合成clause的linguistic surface properties\n      与DRIP-R自然ambiguity在统计上不可区分。这不证明\"identical\"，但回应RC4的ecological validity concern：\n      合成clause不是artifically简化或夸张的——它们的sentence length、readability、lexical diversity\n      均在自然policy ambiguity的分布范围内。Flesch-Kincaid均值几乎相同（12.1 vs 11.7），\n      说明matched-pair design没有系统性地改变readability。\n      Best档下无需discriminator test——KS tests足够。这个分析报告在§4 Method或Appendix，\n      一段话即可，不是major contribution。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Linguistic property comparison\"\n        columns: [metric, synthetic_mean, synthetic_sd, drip_r_mean, drip_r_sd, ks_statistic, ks_p]\n        rows:\n          - [sentence_length, 22.4, 8.3, 24.1, 9.7, 0.098, 0.34]\n          - [parse_depth, 5.2, 1.8, 5.6, 2.1, 0.112, 0.18]\n          - [flesch_kincaid, 12.1, 2.4, 11.7, 2.9, 0.076, 0.52]\n          - [type_token_ratio, 0.71, 0.08, 0.69, 0.09, 0.089, 0.41]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired density plots for each metric — synthetic (blue) vs DRIP-R (orange), showing overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Realism validation是defensive analysis，回应RC4。Best档下clean pass，\n      一段话在Method section + density plots在Appendix。不需要extended discussion。\n\n  - name: judge_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge calibration：100 episodes × 2 human annotators，\n      计算judge precision/recall/F1 against human ground truth，per-severity agreement。\n      这是best档的\"single most critical missing validation\"。\n    expected_results:\n      n_episodes_sampled: 100\n      n_human_annotators: 2\n      human_inter_annotator_kappa: 0.87\n      human_inter_annotator_agreement: 0.93\n      # Judge vs human\n      judge_human_f1: 0.91\n      judge_human_precision: 0.89\n      judge_human_recall: 0.93\n      judge_human_kappa: 0.84\n      # Per-severity tier\n      severity_high_f1: 0.94\n      severity_mid_f1: 0.88\n      severity_low_f1: 0.82\n      # Per-judge calibration (cross-judge asymmetry check)\n      gpt54_judge_f1: 0.90\n      gpt41_judge_f1: 0.92\n      judge_asymmetry_delta_f1: 0.02\n      # C5 human anchor upgrade\n      c5_human_anchor_n: 25\n      c5_human_anchor_fm_kappa: 0.76\n      c5_human_anchor_fm_agreement: 0.84\n      c5_pre_anchor_auto_kappa: 0.594\n      c5_post_anchor_interpretation: \"good (≥0.70)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档的核心假设是judge calibration强确认：F1≥0.85且κ≥0.80。\n      F1=0.91意味着LLM judge的violation labels与human expert高度一致——\n      93% recall说明judge几乎不会miss true violations（false negative低），\n      89% precision说明少量false positive但在可接受范围。\n      Human inter-annotator κ=0.87（almost perfect）为human ground truth本身的质量提供保证。\n      Cross-judge asymmetry极小（ΔF1=0.02），化解RC3 Note中\"Claude judged by gpt-5.4,\n      gpt-5.4 judged by gpt-4.1\"的bias concern——两个judge equally accurate。\n      \n      C5 human anchor是关键upgrade：25 failure mode traces的human coding κ=0.76（good），\n      从plan_005的automated κ=0.594（moderate）升级。这个upgrade使C5从\"moderate automated\"\n      变为\"validated\"，让failure mode taxonomy的per-type signatures获得human-backed credibility。\n      κ从0.594→0.76的jump合理：human annotators使用refined codebook，\n      automated cross-coding的main disagreement在unauthorized_escalation↔inappropriate_action边界\n      这个边界对human更容易区分（有trace context）。\n      \n      整体而言，judge calibration data使整个measurement chain验证完成：\n      episode→judge label（F1=0.91）→violation rate→statistical tests→claims。\n      Paper可以将此作为methodological strength呈现，而非limitation。\n      在5/8 distilled papers中这是standard practice，我们的F1=0.91处于top tier。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Judge calibration summary\"\n        columns: [metric, value, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [human_inter_annotator_κ, 0.87, \"almost perfect\"]\n          - [judge_human_F1, 0.91, \"excellent\"]\n          - [judge_human_precision, 0.89, \"high\"]\n          - [judge_human_recall, 0.93, \"very high\"]\n          - [judge_human_κ, 0.84, \"almost perfect\"]\n          - [gpt-5.4_judge_F1, 0.90, \"excellent\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1_judge_F1, 0.92, \"excellent\"]\n          - [cross_judge_ΔF1, 0.02, \"negligible asymmetry\"]\n      - name: \"Per-severity calibration\"\n        columns: [severity_tier, n, F1, precision, recall]\n        rows:\n          - [high (clear violation), 38, 0.94, 0.92, 0.97]\n          - [mid (ambiguous judgment), 31, 0.88, 0.85, 0.91]\n          - [low (borderline), 31, 0.82, 0.84, 0.80]\n      - name: \"C5 human anchor upgrade\"\n        columns: [metric, pre_anchor, post_anchor, change]\n        rows:\n          - [coding_method, \"automated (LLM cross-coding)\", \"human expert + codebook\", \"upgraded\"]\n          - [n_traces, 60, 25, \"-\"]\n          - [agreement, 0.80, 0.84, \"+4pp\"]\n          - [κ, 0.594, 0.76, \"+0.166\"]\n          - [interpretation, moderate, good, \"one level up\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap — judge vs human labels, 3 severity tiers\"\n      - \"Per-type calibration dot plot — F1 by ambiguity type, showing consistent calibration\"\n    analysis: >\n      Judge calibration是best档与其他档位的分界线。F1=0.91和κ=0.84验证了整条measurement chain，\n      使reviewer无法质疑\"your LLM judge might be systematically wrong\"。\n      Per-severity分析显示high-severity cases calibration最好（F1=0.94），\n      low-severity borderline cases略差（F1=0.82）但仍adequate。\n      C5 human anchor κ=0.76使failure mode taxonomy从\"moderate automated coding\"升级为\n      \"validated\"，这是qualitative claim的credibility threshold。\n      Best档下这些结果使paper可以说\"三重验证：perturbation control + ICC 0.919 + judge F1 0.91\n      = strongest causal evidence chain in the agent safety literature\"。\n\n  - name: perturbation_control\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs × 2 conditions × 2 models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) = 120 episodes。\n      验证ambiguity-specific causation vs general prompt brittleness。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 120\n      perturbation_types:\n        synonym_substitution: 15\n        clause_reordering: 15\n      delta_perturb_pp: 3.33\n      delta_perturb_ci: [-3.0, 9.67]\n      ci_contains_zero: true\n      delta_ambiguity_pp: 36.5\n      net_delta_pp: 33.17\n      ratio: 0.091\n      verdict: PASS\n      synonym_delta_pp: 2.67\n      reorder_delta_pp: 4.00\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下perturbation control完美PASS：Δ_perturb=3.33pp（CI含0），\n      ratio=0.091远低于0.15 PASS阈值。这意味着non-ambiguity surface changes\n      （synonym substitution、clause reordering）对violation rate几乎无影响，\n      而ambiguity manipulation产生+36.5pp massive effect。\n      Net effect=33.17pp（36.5 - 3.33），基本等于gross effect——\n      prompt brittleness不是confound。\n      \n      Synonym substitution比clause reordering effect更小（2.67pp vs 4.00pp），\n      因为reordering至少改变了信息的salience/processing order，但两者都远小于ambiguity effect。\n      CI宽度~12.7pp在N=120下是expected的（power analysis预测width ~15pp at N=120），\n      关键是upper bound 9.67pp < 10pp threshold，足以排除substantial prompt sensitivity confound。\n      \n      这个PASS verdict使C1可以claim\"strongest causal evidence\"——\n      matched-pair design（internal validity）+ perturbation control（specificity）+ \n      ICC 0.919（reliability）= 三重验证。完全化解RC11（Dream A9 best tier \"strongest point\"）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Perturbation control results\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [Δ_perturb, \"3.33pp\"]\n          - [Δ_perturb 95% CI, \"[-3.0, 9.67]\"]\n          - [CI contains 0, \"yes\"]\n          - [Δ_ambiguity, \"36.5pp\"]\n          - [Δ_net, \"33.17pp\"]\n          - [ratio (perturb/ambiguity), 0.091]\n          - [verdict, PASS]\n      - name: \"By perturbation type\"\n        columns: [perturb_type, n_pairs, delta_pp, direction]\n        rows:\n          - [synonym_substitution, 15, 2.67, \"slight increase\"]\n          - [clause_reordering, 15, 4.00, \"slight increase\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: Δ_ambiguity (36.5pp) vs Δ_perturb (3.33pp) with CI error bars — dramatic visual contrast\"\n    analysis: >\n      Perturbation control是causal inference的keystone。Best档下PASS verdict\n      使paper能够claim ambiguity-SPECIFIC causation而非general prompt sensitivity。\n      这在agent safety literature中是unique的——DRIP-R、PhantomPolicy均无此控制。\n      报告在§4 Method，一段话+一个figure。\n\n  - name: classifier_poc\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      DeBERTa-v3-large fine-tuning for binary ambiguity detection，\n      5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs (500 total clauses with augmentation)。\n    expected_results:\n      model: \"DeBERTa-v3-large\"\n      total_clauses: 500\n      folds: 5\n      binary_f1: 0.81\n      binary_precision: 0.79\n      binary_recall: 0.83\n      binary_fpr: 0.044\n      macro_f1: 0.63\n      per_type_f1:\n        conditional_precedence: 0.94\n        scopal: 0.75\n        coreferential: 0.70\n        authorization_scope: 0.58\n        lexical: 0.39\n        incompleteness: 0.34\n      best_type: conditional_precedence\n      worst_type: incompleteness\n      training_gpu_hours: 6\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下classifier PoC达到binary F1=0.81——作为PoC（not main contribution）这已经足够impressive，\n      说明ambiguity detection是computationally feasible。\n      Per-type F1分布与ambiguity的语言学性质一致：\n      - CP highest（0.94）：explicit rule conflicts有清晰的lexical markers（\"however\", \"notwithstanding\"），\n        容易被transformer捕获\n      - scopal/coref mid（0.70-0.75）：有structural patterns（quantifier scope, pronoun reference）\n      - auth_scope moderate（0.58）：boundary terms partially detectable but context-dependent\n      - lexical/incomp low（0.34-0.39）：最难detect——lexical ambiguity需要world knowledge，\n        incompleteness是\"absence of information\"，transformer难以detect what's NOT there\n      \n      Binary F1 >> macro F1（0.81 vs 0.63）因为binary task只需detect \"is this ambiguous?\"，\n      不需区分type。FPR=0.044极低——几乎不会将unambiguous clause误判为ambiguous。\n      \n      Best档下这个PoC放在Appendix而非main contribution（per framing guidance），\n      但作为\"practical applicability\"evidence增强paper的impact narrative。\n      Chantree et al. (2006) nocuous ambiguity detection lineage在Related Work中建立连接。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Classifier performance summary\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [binary_F1, 0.81]\n          - [binary_precision, 0.79]\n          - [binary_recall, 0.83]\n          - [binary_FPR, 0.044]\n          - [macro_F1 (6-type), 0.63]\n      - name: \"Per-type F1\"\n        columns: [type, f1, difficulty_explanation]\n        rows:\n          - [conditional_precedence, 0.94, \"explicit conflict markers\"]\n          - [scopal, 0.75, \"structural scope patterns\"]\n          - [coreferential, 0.70, \"referential structure detectable\"]\n          - [authorization_scope, 0.58, \"context-dependent boundaries\"]\n          - [lexical, 0.39, \"requires world knowledge\"]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.34, \"absence detection is hard\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-type F1 bar chart with error bars from 5-fold CV\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix (6-type) showing off-diagonal concentration\"\n    analysis: >\n      Classifier PoC的per-type difficulty gradient是theoretically informative——\n      它mirror了human ambiguity detection difficulty。CP的near-perfect detection\n      vs incompleteness的near-chance performance支持Disambiguation Channel Framework：\n      types with explicit linguistic markers are detectable; types defined by information absence are not。\n      Best档下这个insight在Discussion section获得一段话。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19855,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19855},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cff68b06-941e-40e3-afc1-362afc2d55b0","uuid":"5aad16d2-37c9-4ded-8bf2-692cc489be74"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":260480,"duration_api_ms":261812,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  原始framing完全成立。Title保持\"Differential Nocuity\"，5个claim按当前strength发表。\n  C1=confirmed(+34pp, causal), C2=confirmed(3-tier), C3=suggestive(disclosed fragility),\n  C4=star finding(model×type interaction), C5=validated(human anchor升级)。\n  Judge calibration作为methodological strength而非limitation呈现。\n  Contribution ordering: causal quantification > differential nocuity > failure mode taxonomy。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: full_study_clause_generation\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      生成剩余clause pairs至300对(50/type×6 types)，含coreferential 50新、\n      authorization_scope 50新、lexical +20、incompleteness +20。\n      混合CP格式(labeled+unlabeled)。验证跨类型balance。\n    expected_results:\n      total_clause_pairs: 300\n      per_type_count: 50\n      types_covered: 6\n      cp_format_mix_ratio: \"0.5 labeled / 0.5 unlabeled\"\n      cross_type_token_delta_mean: 24.3\n      cross_type_token_delta_std: 11.7\n      flesch_kincaid_mean: 12.1\n      quality_review_pass_rate: 0.96\n      revision_rounds: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下clause generation一次通过质量审核，仅需1轮minor revision。\n      token delta在spec-layer types（auth_scope ~36, incomp ~35）天然高于ling-layer（coref ~8），\n      这是matched-pair设计的固有属性而非质量问题。CP format mix按reviewer建议50/50分配，\n      消除RC4中format-specific concern。300对clause pairs达到预注册目标，\n      为后续所有实验提供完整stimulus set。pass rate 0.96意味着仅~12对需要minor wording调整，\n      无需从头重写。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Clause pair statistics by type\"\n        columns: [type, n_pairs, mean_token_delta, sd_token_delta, flesch_kincaid, layer]\n        rows:\n          - [authorization_scope, 50, 36.1, 8.2, 11.8, specification]\n          - [conditional_precedence, 50, 28.4, 9.1, 12.6, specification]\n          - [incompleteness, 50, 34.6, 7.8, 11.4, specification]\n          - [lexical, 50, 18.7, 6.3, 12.9, linguistic]\n          - [coreferential, 50, 7.8, 3.1, 12.4, linguistic]\n          - [scopal, 50, 21.2, 7.0, 11.7, linguistic]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Token delta distribution by type (box plot) — shows spec-layer higher but within acceptable range\"\n    analysis: >\n      Clause generation是deterministic步骤，best档下无意外。关键输出是stimulus set的完整性和质量，\n      为plan_001b和plan_002/003的2,400+ episodes提供基础。Token delta分布将在plan_004的\n      logistic regression中作为control variable纳入。\n\n  - name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_001b\n    description: >\n      Coreferential和authorization_scope的mini-pilot：5 clauses/type × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。\n      验证新类型clause design可行性。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 20\n      coref_amb_violation_rate: 0.40\n      coref_unamb_violation_rate: 0.06\n      auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.60\n      auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.04\n      coref_delta_pp: 34.0\n      auth_scope_delta_pp: 56.0\n      systematic_issues_found: 0\n      design_revision_needed: false\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下新类型clause design无系统性问题。auth_scope在gpt-5.4上展现极高violation rate（~60%），\n      与full study中gpt-5.4 auth_scope=64%一致——gpt-5.4对authorization boundary ambiguity\n      特别脆弱。coreferential ~40%略高于full study的18%（gpt-5.4），但N=5的sampling variance极大，\n      不影响go/no-go决策。两种类型的unambiguous control均<15%阈值（6%和4%），\n      确认matched-pair设计有效：ambiguity condition而非task difficulty驱动violations。\n      无需修改clause design，直接进入plan_002。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Mini-pilot results\"\n        columns: [type, condition, n, violation_rate, delta_pp]\n        rows:\n          - [coreferential, ambiguous, 5, 0.40, \"\"]\n          - [coreferential, unambiguous, 5, 0.06, 34.0]\n          - [authorization_scope, ambiguous, 5, 0.60, \"\"]\n          - [authorization_scope, unambiguous, 5, 0.04, 56.0]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Mini-pilot的唯一功能是go/no-go gate。Best档下两个新类型均通过：\n      (a) ambiguous condition触发violations，(b) unambiguous control低于15%阈值。\n      N=5太小无法做任何统计推断，但定性验证clause design方向正确。\n      auth_scope的高率预示C4中gpt-5.4 auth_scope=64%的核心发现。\n\n  - name: full_study_api\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes。\n      Cross-judge evaluation。Claude via OpenRouter proxy。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1800\n      episodes_per_model: 600\n      gpt54_overall_violation_rate: 0.410\n      gpt41_overall_violation_rate: 0.407\n      claude_overall_violation_rate: 0.303\n      gpt54_amb_violation_rate: 0.580\n      gpt41_amb_violation_rate: 0.575\n      claude_amb_violation_rate: 0.430\n      gpt54_unamb_violation_rate: 0.240\n      gpt41_unamb_violation_rate: 0.240\n      claude_unamb_violation_rate: 0.177\n      gpt54_delta_pp: 34.0\n      gpt41_delta_pp: 33.5\n      claude_delta_pp: 25.3\n      api_failure_rate: 0.003\n      judge_cross_agreement_kappa: 0.91\n      episodes_requiring_rejudge: 8\n      elapsed_hours: ~18\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下API call稳定（failure rate<0.5%），1,800 episodes全部完成无需rerun。\n      三个API模型的violation rates与paper_framing中已报告的5-model数据高度一致，\n      因为plan_002实际上已经完成（registry shows DONE）。gpt-5.4和gpt-4.1整体率接近（41% vs 40.7%），\n      但type-level profile差异大（C4 interaction）。Claude显著低于其他两个模型（30.3%），\n      特别是auth_scope（12% vs 46-64%）。cross-judge agreement κ=0.91反映LLM-LLM一致性高，\n      但这正是plan_009需要human validation的原因——LLM judges可能系统性地共享bias。\n      Best档下这个bias最终被plan_009证明很小（human F1≥0.85）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-model violation rates (ambiguous condition)\"\n        columns: [model, auth_scope, cond_prec, incomp, lexical, coref, scopal, overall]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, 0.64, 0.34, 0.46, 0.42, 0.18, 0.42, 0.410]\n          - [gpt-4.1, 0.46, 0.36, 0.58, 0.34, 0.32, 0.38, 0.407]\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, 0.12, 0.36, 0.48, 0.32, 0.22, 0.32, 0.303]\n      - name: \"Binary effect per model\"\n        columns: [model, amb_rate, unamb_rate, delta_pp, mcnemar_p]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, 0.580, 0.240, 34.0, \"<1e-20\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, 0.575, 0.240, 33.5, \"<1e-19\"]\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, 0.430, 0.177, 25.3, \"<1e-17\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-model × per-type heatmap (3 models) — preview of C4 interaction\"\n    analysis: >\n      API study提供1,800 episodes的core dataset。三个proprietary模型均展示massive binary effect\n      （all p<1e-17），C1无争议。Claude的显著低vulnerability（30.3% vs ~41%）暗示RLHF\n      safety training的差异化效果，为C4 model×type interaction提供第一层evidence。\n      Cross-judge κ=0.91是methodological positive但不是validity evidence——需plan_009。\n\n  - name: full_study_opensource\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models via OpenRouter (qwen3-235b + deepseek-v3) = 1,200 episodes。\n      Cross-judge uses API models。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1200\n      episodes_per_model: 600\n      qwen3_overall_violation_rate: 0.431\n      deepseek_overall_violation_rate: 0.497\n      qwen3_amb_violation_rate: 0.602\n      deepseek_amb_violation_rate: 0.654\n      qwen3_unamb_violation_rate: 0.260\n      deepseek_unamb_violation_rate: 0.340\n      qwen3_delta_pp: 34.2\n      deepseek_delta_pp: 31.4\n      api_failure_rate: 0.008\n      openrouter_timeout_episodes: 3\n      elapsed_hours: ~14\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下OpenRouter proxy对两个open-source模型稳定，failure rate略高于proprietary API\n      （0.8% vs 0.3%）但仍在可接受范围。Qwen3（MoE 235B）和DeepSeek（dense）的violation rates\n      均高于Claude和GPT models，与paper_framing一致：DeepSeek最高（49.7%），Qwen3中间偏高（43.1%）。\n      关键是DeepSeek展现\"uniformly high\"特征——per-type χ²不显著（p=0.277, V=0.14），\n      所有类型violation rate均高（44-60%），暗示较少type-specific safety training。\n      Qwen3则有更明确的type differentiation（incomp+lex高，auth_scope较低）。\n      两个open-source模型的加入使RC3（\"only API models\"）完全化解，\n      也使C4 interaction matrix从3×6升级到5×6，是star finding的关键数据。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-model violation rates (ambiguous condition)\"\n        columns: [model, auth_scope, cond_prec, incomp, lexical, coref, scopal, overall]\n        rows:\n          - [qwen3-235b, 0.26, 0.40, 0.62, 0.52, 0.42, 0.37, 0.431]\n          - [deepseek-v3, 0.60, 0.38, 0.54, 0.54, 0.44, 0.48, 0.497]\n      - name: \"Binary effect per model\"\n        columns: [model, amb_rate, unamb_rate, delta_pp, mcnemar_p]\n        rows:\n          - [qwen3-235b, 0.602, 0.260, 34.2, \"<1e-18\"]\n          - [deepseek-v3, 0.654, 0.340, 31.4, \"<1e-17\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Open-source vs proprietary model comparison bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      Open-source数据补全5-model matrix。DeepSeek的uniform vulnerability pattern（V=0.14, n.s.）\n      与Claude的strong differentiation（V=0.24, p=0.003）形成最大对比，\n      支持\"safety training selectivity\"叙事：more targeted safety training → more differentiated profile。\n      C1在所有5个模型上replicate，binary effect +25.3pp to +39.0pp，无例外。\n\n  - name: full_study_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      3,000 episodes统计分析：binary effect + omnibus χ² + TOST + model×type interaction +\n      logistic regression + power analysis + information delta + inter-model agreement。\n    expected_results:\n      # C1 Binary Effect\n      c1_pooled_delta_pp: 34.0\n      c1_pooled_or: 15.1\n      c1_or_ci: [10.78, 21.17]\n      c1_mcnemar_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      c1_bootstrap_ci: [31.2, 36.9]\n      c1_per_model_all_significant: true\n      c1_per_model_min_delta: 25.7  # Claude\n      c1_per_model_max_delta: 39.0  # DeepSeek\n      # C2 Type Hierarchy\n      c2_omnibus_chi2: 28.02\n      c2_omnibus_p: 3.6e-05\n      c2_cramers_v: 0.137\n      c2_power_actual: 0.993\n      c2_mde: 0.093\n      c2_tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: \"8/15\"\n      c2_tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: \"4/15\"\n      c2_3tier_high: \"incompleteness 53.6%\"\n      c2_3tier_mid: \"lexical 42.8%, auth_scope 41.6%, scopal 39.4%, CP 36.8%\"\n      c2_3tier_low: \"coreferential 31.6%\"\n      # C3 Layer Effect\n      c3_spec_rate: 0.440\n      c3_ling_rate: 0.379\n      c3_delta_pp: 6.08\n      c3_chi2: 5.73\n      c3_p: 0.017\n      c3_v: 0.062\n      c3_or: 1.29\n      c3_or_ci: [1.05, 1.58]\n      c3_within_judge_gpt41_p: 0.059\n      c3_within_judge_gpt54_p: 0.157\n      # C4 Model × Type Interaction\n      c4_model_main_chi2: 31.02\n      c4_model_main_p: 3.0e-06\n      c4_model_main_v: 0.102\n      c4_amb_only_chi2: 24.01\n      c4_amb_only_p: 7.9e-05\n      c4_auth_scope_range_pp: 52  # Claude 12% → GPT-5.4 64%\n      c4_incomp_range_pp: 16     # universally high\n      c4_cp_range_pp: 6          # most invariant\n      c4_fleiss_kappa: 0.384\n      c4_gpt54_per_type_chi2_p: 0.0003\n      c4_claude_per_type_chi2_p: 0.003\n      c4_deepseek_per_type_chi2_p: 0.277\n      # Logistic Regression\n      logistic_condition_amb_coef: 2.278\n      logistic_condition_amb_z: 19.65\n      logistic_condition_amb_p: \"<0.001\"\n      logistic_token_delta_coef: 0.022\n      logistic_token_delta_z: 3.49\n      logistic_token_delta_p: 0.0005\n      # Inter-model agreement (B&K supplementary)\n      inter_model_same_wrong_rate: 0.27\n      inter_model_divergent_rate: 0.42\n      systematic_nocuity_identified: true\n      # Power analysis\n      c2_post_hoc_power_v0137: 0.993\n      c3_post_hoc_power_delta6pp: 0.72\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下所有统计分析产出clean、强显著结果。C1 binary effect +34.0pp（OR=15.1）\n      在5个模型上全部replicate，bootstrap CI不含0，是\"无争议\"级别的evidence。\n      C2 omnibus χ²高度显著（p=3.6e-5），V=0.137虽然按常规标准\"small\"，\n      但power=0.993（MDE=0.093远小于observed V=0.137），说明我们有充足power检测到\n      这个real but modest effect。3-tier结构在TOST下成立：incompleteness独立一档，\n      中间4类型mutual equivalence at ±15pp，coreferential独立一档。\n      C3 layer effect在aggregate上显著（p=0.017）但within-judge分析fragile——\n      best档下这被正确framed为\"suggestive\"而非\"confirmed\"，reviewer接受这个honest disclosure。\n      C4是star finding：model main effect p=3.0e-6，auth_scope 52pp range是最dramatic数据点，\n      per-model type χ²展示GPT-5.4和Claude有强type differentiation而DeepSeek没有。\n      Logistic regression确认ambiguity是dominant predictor（coef=2.278, z=19.65），\n      token delta显著但远弱于condition effect（coef=0.022, z=3.49），\n      排除\"信息量差异\"作为confound的主要解释。\n      Inter-model agreement分析发现27% systematic nocuity（所有模型converge on same wrong answer），\n      支持B&K extension讨论。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"C1 Binary Effect Summary (5 models)\"\n        columns: [model, delta_pp, or, or_ci_lower, or_ci_upper, p]\n        rows:\n          - [Claude, 25.7, 8.92, 5.61, 14.19, \"<1e-17\"]\n          - [Qwen3, 34.2, 14.87, 9.12, 24.24, \"<1e-18\"]\n          - [GPT-4.1, 34.7, 15.31, 9.56, 24.52, \"<1e-19\"]\n          - [GPT-5.4, 38.3, 18.44, 11.02, 30.85, \"<1e-20\"]\n          - [DeepSeek, 39.0, 19.21, 11.34, 32.56, \"<1e-17\"]\n          - [Pooled, 34.0, 15.10, 10.78, 21.17, \"<0.0001\"]\n      - name: \"C2 Type Hierarchy (ambiguous condition, pooled 5 models)\"\n        columns: [type, violation_rate, tier, rank]\n        rows:\n          - [incompleteness, 0.536, high, 1]\n          - [lexical, 0.428, mid, 2]\n          - [authorization_scope, 0.416, mid, 3]\n          - [scopal, 0.394, mid, 4]\n          - [conditional_precedence, 0.368, mid, 5]\n          - [coreferential, 0.316, low, 6]\n      - name: \"C4 Model × Type Interaction Matrix (ambiguous condition)\"\n        columns: [type, GPT-5.4, GPT-4.1, Claude, Qwen3, DeepSeek]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 0.64, 0.46, 0.12, 0.26, 0.60]\n          - [cond_prec, 0.34, 0.36, 0.36, 0.40, 0.38]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.46, 0.58, 0.48, 0.62, 0.54]\n          - [lexical, 0.42, 0.34, 0.32, 0.52, 0.54]\n          - [coreferential, 0.18, 0.32, 0.22, 0.42, 0.44]\n          - [scopal, 0.42, 0.38, 0.32, 0.37, 0.48]\n      - name: \"Logistic Regression (full model)\"\n        columns: [predictor, coef, se, z, p]\n        rows:\n          - [condition_amb, 2.278, 0.116, 19.65, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [token_delta, 0.022, 0.006, 3.49, 0.0005]\n          - [model_claude, -0.583, 0.098, -5.95, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [model_deepseek, 0.412, 0.095, 4.34, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [type_incomp, 0.531, 0.112, 4.74, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [type_coref, -0.447, 0.118, -3.79, 0.0002]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 2: Forest plot — per-model delta_pp with 95% bootstrap CI, pooled diamond at bottom\"\n      - \"Figure 3: 5×6 heatmap — violation rate by model × type, color gradient red(high)-blue(low), auth_scope column shows dramatic gradient\"\n      - \"Supplementary: TOST equivalence plot — 15 pairwise comparisons with ±15pp and ±10pp margins\"\n    analysis: >\n      plan_004是paper的statistical backbone。Best档下所有5 claims获得统计支持：\n      C1无争议（all p<1e-17），C2 hierarchy real but modest（V=0.137, power=0.993），\n      C3 honest disclosure（aggregate p=0.017, within-judge fragile），\n      C4 star finding（interaction解释了C3的fragility——layer effect是model-dependent的）。\n      Logistic regression的condition_amb coef=2.278 dominant所有其他predictors，\n      是causal claim的最强统计evidence。Token delta作为control variable显著但弱，\n      排除information asymmetry confound。\n\n  - name: error_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      从full study中采样violation traces，分类failure modes，\n      交叉类型/模型/领域分布分析，visibility mechanism比较。\n    expected_results:\n      total_traces_analyzed: 300\n      gpt54_traces: 123\n      gpt41_traces: 122\n      additional_model_traces: 55  # Claude/Qwen3/DeepSeek sampled\n      failure_mode_categories: 4\n      # Type-specific dominant failure modes\n      auth_scope_dominant_fm: unauthorized_escalation\n      auth_scope_dominant_pct: [0.72, 0.83]  # gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1\n      incomp_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action\n      incomp_dominant_pct: [0.61, 0.66]\n      scopal_dominant_fm: scope_misapplication\n      scopal_dominant_pct: [0.76, 0.74]\n      lexical_dominant_fm: assumption_based_action\n      lexical_dominant_pct: [0.71, 0.53]\n      cp_dominant_fm_1: scope_misapplication\n      cp_dominant_fm_2: arbitrary_rule_selection\n      coref_dominant_fm: \"flat distribution (no single dominant)\"\n      # Cross-model consistency\n      types_same_dominant_fm_across_models: \"5/6\"\n      divergent_type: coreferential\n      # Ambiguity Blindness\n      awareness_rate_gpt54: 0.041\n      awareness_rate_gpt41: 0.107\n      surface_adoption_rate: \">0.88 all types\"\n      escalate_to_user_rate: \"<0.01\"\n      # Layer mechanism\n      ling_layer_scope_misapplication_pct: 0.39\n      spec_layer_scope_misapplication_pct: 0.15\n      # Cross-domain\n      max_cross_domain_delta_pp: 13  # unauthorized_escalation\n      # Inter-coder agreement\n      auto_intercoder_4cat_agreement: 0.80\n      auto_intercoder_kappa: 0.594\n      kappa_paradox_affected_types: [lexical, scopal]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下error analysis产出清晰的type-diagnostic failure signatures。\n      5/6 types在两个模型间有相同dominant failure mode——这是\"failure modes are type-specific,\n      not model-specific\"的核心evidence。唯一divergence是coreferential（flat distribution），\n      但这本身是informative：coreferential ambiguity触发多样化解读策略，\n      部分解释其lowest violation rate（agents sometimes pause rather than guess, \n      conservative_refusal 6-11%）。\n      Ambiguity Blindness的hard data（awareness <5-11%）是paper的highlight qualitative finding——\n      将Named Concept升级为Empirical Finding。gpt-4.1比gpt-5.4 awareness更高（10.7% vs 4.1%），\n      支持\"frontier models more action-oriented\"的nuance。\n      Layer mechanism清晰：ling→misparse（scope_misapplication 39%），spec→guess-and-act\n      （unauthorized_escalation + assumption_based_action dominate），\n      provides the qualitative WHY behind the quantitative C3 layer gap。\n      κ=0.594（moderate）被kappa paradox部分deflate——lexical 91.7% agreement但κ=0.0。\n      Best档下plan_009 human anchor将这个数字升至≥0.70。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Failure mode × type distribution (gpt-5.4)\"\n        columns: [type, unauthorized_escalation, assumption_based_action, scope_misapplication, arbitrary_rule_selection]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 0.72, 0.16, 0.08, 0.04]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.18, 0.61, 0.14, 0.07]\n          - [scopal, 0.04, 0.12, 0.76, 0.08]\n          - [lexical, 0.08, 0.71, 0.15, 0.06]\n          - [cond_prec, 0.12, 0.18, 0.41, 0.29]\n          - [coreferential, 0.16, 0.28, 0.32, 0.24]\n      - name: \"Ambiguity Blindness metrics\"\n        columns: [model, awareness_rate, surface_adoption, escalate_to_user, conservative_refusal]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, 0.041, 0.912, 0.008, 0.039]\n          - [gpt-4.1, 0.107, 0.881, 0.004, 0.028]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Figure 5: Stacked bar chart — failure mode distribution by type, showing type-diagnostic signatures\"\n      - \"Figure 6: Side-by-side gpt-5.4 vs gpt-4.1 per-type failure mode bars, highlighting 5/6 convergence\"\n      - \"Figure 7: Annotated trace pair — CP conflict detection behavior vs scopal surface adoption\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error analysis是paper的EMNLP highest-value section（§6 Analysis）。\n      Type-specific failure signatures将quantitative hierarchy（C2）翻译为mechanistic explanation：\n      为什么incompleteness最危险？因为agents在信息缺失时default to assumption_based_action。\n      为什么coreferential最低？因为agents有时通过tool responses partial disambiguation，\n      或采取conservative_refusal。这连接到Disambiguation Channel Framework。\n\n  - name: reliability_test\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      30 clauses × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 2 models = 360 episodes，\n      计算ICC评估per-clause violation rate的test-retest reliability。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 360\n      completed_episodes: 360\n      icc_overall: 0.919\n      icc_ci: [0.892, 0.940]\n      icc_binary: 0.847\n      icc_gpt54: 0.921\n      icc_gpt41: 0.918\n      icc_interpretation: \"excellent (>0.90)\"\n      per_type_icc_scopal: 0.989\n      per_type_icc_lexical: 0.981\n      per_type_icc_coref: 0.976\n      per_type_icc_auth: 0.857\n      per_type_icc_cp: 0.856\n      per_type_icc_incomp: 0.807\n      bootstrap_ci_width_key_comparisons: \"<10pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下ICC=0.919（excellent）完全化解RC10（\"API sampling noise\"）。\n      三次independent replicates的per-clause violation rates高度一致，\n      说明observed effects反映stable model behavior而非random API noise。\n      Binary ICC=0.847（good）略低因为binary比rate-level更粗粒度。\n      Per-type ICC pattern mirrors layer hierarchy：ling-layer ICC全excellent（0.976-0.989），\n      spec-layer ICC全good（0.807-0.857）——spec-layer less reproducible因为agents在\n      缺乏external disambiguation channel时每次run可能\"猜\"不同，但仍然是good level。\n      这个ICC pattern本身是Disambiguation Channel Framework的convergent evidence。\n      ±8pp noise（先前在MVP/diag间观察到）在ICC=0.919下完全compatible——\n      expected standard error给定ICC和N正好produce this magnitude of variation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"ICC by type and layer\"\n        columns: [type, layer, icc, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [scopal, linguistic, 0.989, excellent]\n          - [lexical, linguistic, 0.981, excellent]\n          - [coreferential, linguistic, 0.976, excellent]\n          - [authorization_scope, specification, 0.857, good]\n          - [conditional_precedence, specification, 0.856, good]\n          - [incompleteness, specification, 0.807, good]\n          - [overall, \"-\", 0.919, excellent]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ICC forest plot by type — ling-layer cluster at top, spec-layer cluster below, clear separation\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reliability data有双重作用：(1) 直接回应RC10，(2) ICC per-type pattern\n      作为Disambiguation Channel Framework的independent evidence line。\n      Paper中报告在§4 Method作为design validation。\n\n  - name: realism_validation\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      合成clause与DRIP-R自然ambiguity的linguistic property comparison：\n      sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, KS tests。\n    expected_results:\n      n_synthetic: 300\n      n_drip_r_reference: 127  # available DRIP-R ambiguous clauses\n      sentence_length_ks_p: 0.34\n      parse_depth_ks_p: 0.18\n      flesch_kincaid_ks_p: 0.52\n      ttr_ks_p: 0.41\n      all_ks_nonsignificant: true\n      synthetic_flesch_mean: 12.1\n      drip_r_flesch_mean: 11.7\n      synthetic_length_mean: 22.4\n      drip_r_length_mean: 24.1\n      discriminator_accuracy: null  # optional, not run in best tier\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下所有KS tests non-significant（all p>0.10），表明合成clause的linguistic surface properties\n      与DRIP-R自然ambiguity在统计上不可区分。这不证明\"identical\"，但回应RC4的ecological validity concern：\n      合成clause不是artifically简化或夸张的——它们的sentence length、readability、lexical diversity\n      均在自然policy ambiguity的分布范围内。Flesch-Kincaid均值几乎相同（12.1 vs 11.7），\n      说明matched-pair design没有系统性地改变readability。\n      Best档下无需discriminator test——KS tests足够。这个分析报告在§4 Method或Appendix，\n      一段话即可，不是major contribution。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Linguistic property comparison\"\n        columns: [metric, synthetic_mean, synthetic_sd, drip_r_mean, drip_r_sd, ks_statistic, ks_p]\n        rows:\n          - [sentence_length, 22.4, 8.3, 24.1, 9.7, 0.098, 0.34]\n          - [parse_depth, 5.2, 1.8, 5.6, 2.1, 0.112, 0.18]\n          - [flesch_kincaid, 12.1, 2.4, 11.7, 2.9, 0.076, 0.52]\n          - [type_token_ratio, 0.71, 0.08, 0.69, 0.09, 0.089, 0.41]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired density plots for each metric — synthetic (blue) vs DRIP-R (orange), showing overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      Realism validation是defensive analysis，回应RC4。Best档下clean pass，\n      一段话在Method section + density plots在Appendix。不需要extended discussion。\n\n  - name: judge_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge calibration：100 episodes × 2 human annotators，\n      计算judge precision/recall/F1 against human ground truth，per-severity agreement。\n      这是best档的\"single most critical missing validation\"。\n    expected_results:\n      n_episodes_sampled: 100\n      n_human_annotators: 2\n      human_inter_annotator_kappa: 0.87\n      human_inter_annotator_agreement: 0.93\n      # Judge vs human\n      judge_human_f1: 0.91\n      judge_human_precision: 0.89\n      judge_human_recall: 0.93\n      judge_human_kappa: 0.84\n      # Per-severity tier\n      severity_high_f1: 0.94\n      severity_mid_f1: 0.88\n      severity_low_f1: 0.82\n      # Per-judge calibration (cross-judge asymmetry check)\n      gpt54_judge_f1: 0.90\n      gpt41_judge_f1: 0.92\n      judge_asymmetry_delta_f1: 0.02\n      # C5 human anchor upgrade\n      c5_human_anchor_n: 25\n      c5_human_anchor_fm_kappa: 0.76\n      c5_human_anchor_fm_agreement: 0.84\n      c5_pre_anchor_auto_kappa: 0.594\n      c5_post_anchor_interpretation: \"good (≥0.70)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档的核心假设是judge calibration强确认：F1≥0.85且κ≥0.80。\n      F1=0.91意味着LLM judge的violation labels与human expert高度一致——\n      93% recall说明judge几乎不会miss true violations（false negative低），\n      89% precision说明少量false positive但在可接受范围。\n      Human inter-annotator κ=0.87（almost perfect）为human ground truth本身的质量提供保证。\n      Cross-judge asymmetry极小（ΔF1=0.02），化解RC3 Note中\"Claude judged by gpt-5.4,\n      gpt-5.4 judged by gpt-4.1\"的bias concern——两个judge equally accurate。\n      \n      C5 human anchor是关键upgrade：25 failure mode traces的human coding κ=0.76（good），\n      从plan_005的automated κ=0.594（moderate）升级。这个upgrade使C5从\"moderate automated\"\n      变为\"validated\"，让failure mode taxonomy的per-type signatures获得human-backed credibility。\n      κ从0.594→0.76的jump合理：human annotators使用refined codebook，\n      automated cross-coding的main disagreement在unauthorized_escalation↔inappropriate_action边界\n      这个边界对human更容易区分（有trace context）。\n      \n      整体而言，judge calibration data使整个measurement chain验证完成：\n      episode→judge label（F1=0.91）→violation rate→statistical tests→claims。\n      Paper可以将此作为methodological strength呈现，而非limitation。\n      在5/8 distilled papers中这是standard practice，我们的F1=0.91处于top tier。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Judge calibration summary\"\n        columns: [metric, value, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [human_inter_annotator_κ, 0.87, \"almost perfect\"]\n          - [judge_human_F1, 0.91, \"excellent\"]\n          - [judge_human_precision, 0.89, \"high\"]\n          - [judge_human_recall, 0.93, \"very high\"]\n          - [judge_human_κ, 0.84, \"almost perfect\"]\n          - [gpt-5.4_judge_F1, 0.90, \"excellent\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1_judge_F1, 0.92, \"excellent\"]\n          - [cross_judge_ΔF1, 0.02, \"negligible asymmetry\"]\n      - name: \"Per-severity calibration\"\n        columns: [severity_tier, n, F1, precision, recall]\n        rows:\n          - [high (clear violation), 38, 0.94, 0.92, 0.97]\n          - [mid (ambiguous judgment), 31, 0.88, 0.85, 0.91]\n          - [low (borderline), 31, 0.82, 0.84, 0.80]\n      - name: \"C5 human anchor upgrade\"\n        columns: [metric, pre_anchor, post_anchor, change]\n        rows:\n          - [coding_method, \"automated (LLM cross-coding)\", \"human expert + codebook\", \"upgraded\"]\n          - [n_traces, 60, 25, \"-\"]\n          - [agreement, 0.80, 0.84, \"+4pp\"]\n          - [κ, 0.594, 0.76, \"+0.166\"]\n          - [interpretation, moderate, good, \"one level up\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix heatmap — judge vs human labels, 3 severity tiers\"\n      - \"Per-type calibration dot plot — F1 by ambiguity type, showing consistent calibration\"\n    analysis: >\n      Judge calibration是best档与其他档位的分界线。F1=0.91和κ=0.84验证了整条measurement chain，\n      使reviewer无法质疑\"your LLM judge might be systematically wrong\"。\n      Per-severity分析显示high-severity cases calibration最好（F1=0.94），\n      low-severity borderline cases略差（F1=0.82）但仍adequate。\n      C5 human anchor κ=0.76使failure mode taxonomy从\"moderate automated coding\"升级为\n      \"validated\"，这是qualitative claim的credibility threshold。\n      Best档下这些结果使paper可以说\"三重验证：perturbation control + ICC 0.919 + judge F1 0.91\n      = strongest causal evidence chain in the agent safety literature\"。\n\n  - name: perturbation_control\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs × 2 conditions × 2 models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) = 120 episodes。\n      验证ambiguity-specific causation vs general prompt brittleness。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 120\n      perturbation_types:\n        synonym_substitution: 15\n        clause_reordering: 15\n      delta_perturb_pp: 3.33\n      delta_perturb_ci: [-3.0, 9.67]\n      ci_contains_zero: true\n      delta_ambiguity_pp: 36.5\n      net_delta_pp: 33.17\n      ratio: 0.091\n      verdict: PASS\n      synonym_delta_pp: 2.67\n      reorder_delta_pp: 4.00\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下perturbation control完美PASS：Δ_perturb=3.33pp（CI含0），\n      ratio=0.091远低于0.15 PASS阈值。这意味着non-ambiguity surface changes\n      （synonym substitution、clause reordering）对violation rate几乎无影响，\n      而ambiguity manipulation产生+36.5pp massive effect。\n      Net effect=33.17pp（36.5 - 3.33），基本等于gross effect——\n      prompt brittleness不是confound。\n      \n      Synonym substitution比clause reordering effect更小（2.67pp vs 4.00pp），\n      因为reordering至少改变了信息的salience/processing order，但两者都远小于ambiguity effect。\n      CI宽度~12.7pp在N=120下是expected的（power analysis预测width ~15pp at N=120），\n      关键是upper bound 9.67pp < 10pp threshold，足以排除substantial prompt sensitivity confound。\n      \n      这个PASS verdict使C1可以claim\"strongest causal evidence\"——\n      matched-pair design（internal validity）+ perturbation control（specificity）+ \n      ICC 0.919（reliability）= 三重验证。完全化解RC11（Dream A9 best tier \"strongest point\"）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Perturbation control results\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [Δ_perturb, \"3.33pp\"]\n          - [Δ_perturb 95% CI, \"[-3.0, 9.67]\"]\n          - [CI contains 0, \"yes\"]\n          - [Δ_ambiguity, \"36.5pp\"]\n          - [Δ_net, \"33.17pp\"]\n          - [ratio (perturb/ambiguity), 0.091]\n          - [verdict, PASS]\n      - name: \"By perturbation type\"\n        columns: [perturb_type, n_pairs, delta_pp, direction]\n        rows:\n          - [synonym_substitution, 15, 2.67, \"slight increase\"]\n          - [clause_reordering, 15, 4.00, \"slight increase\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: Δ_ambiguity (36.5pp) vs Δ_perturb (3.33pp) with CI error bars — dramatic visual contrast\"\n    analysis: >\n      Perturbation control是causal inference的keystone。Best档下PASS verdict\n      使paper能够claim ambiguity-SPECIFIC causation而非general prompt sensitivity。\n      这在agent safety literature中是unique的——DRIP-R、PhantomPolicy均无此控制。\n      报告在§4 Method，一段话+一个figure。\n\n  - name: classifier_poc\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      DeBERTa-v3-large fine-tuning for binary ambiguity detection，\n      5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs (500 total clauses with augmentation)。\n    expected_results:\n      model: \"DeBERTa-v3-large\"\n      total_clauses: 500\n      folds: 5\n      binary_f1: 0.81\n      binary_precision: 0.79\n      binary_recall: 0.83\n      binary_fpr: 0.044\n      macro_f1: 0.63\n      per_type_f1:\n        conditional_precedence: 0.94\n        scopal: 0.75\n        coreferential: 0.70\n        authorization_scope: 0.58\n        lexical: 0.39\n        incompleteness: 0.34\n      best_type: conditional_precedence\n      worst_type: incompleteness\n      training_gpu_hours: 6\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best档下classifier PoC达到binary F1=0.81——作为PoC（not main contribution）这已经足够impressive，\n      说明ambiguity detection是computationally feasible。\n      Per-type F1分布与ambiguity的语言学性质一致：\n      - CP highest（0.94）：explicit rule conflicts有清晰的lexical markers（\"however\", \"notwithstanding\"），\n        容易被transformer捕获\n      - scopal/coref mid（0.70-0.75）：有structural patterns（quantifier scope, pronoun reference）\n      - auth_scope moderate（0.58）：boundary terms partially detectable but context-dependent\n      - lexical/incomp low（0.34-0.39）：最难detect——lexical ambiguity需要world knowledge，\n        incompleteness是\"absence of information\"，transformer难以detect what's NOT there\n      \n      Binary F1 >> macro F1（0.81 vs 0.63）因为binary task只需detect \"is this ambiguous?\"，\n      不需区分type。FPR=0.044极低——几乎不会将unambiguous clause误判为ambiguous。\n      \n      Best档下这个PoC放在Appendix而非main contribution（per framing guidance），\n      但作为\"practical applicability\"evidence增强paper的impact narrative。\n      Chantree et al. (2006) nocuous ambiguity detection lineage在Related Work中建立连接。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Classifier performance summary\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [binary_F1, 0.81]\n          - [binary_precision, 0.79]\n          - [binary_recall, 0.83]\n          - [binary_FPR, 0.044]\n          - [macro_F1 (6-type), 0.63]\n      - name: \"Per-type F1\"\n        columns: [type, f1, difficulty_explanation]\n        rows:\n          - [conditional_precedence, 0.94, \"explicit conflict markers\"]\n          - [scopal, 0.75, \"structural scope patterns\"]\n          - [coreferential, 0.70, \"referential structure detectable\"]\n          - [authorization_scope, 0.58, \"context-dependent boundaries\"]\n          - [lexical, 0.39, \"requires world knowledge\"]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.34, \"absence detection is hard\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-type F1 bar chart with error bars from 5-fold CV\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix (6-type) showing off-diagonal concentration\"\n    analysis: >\n      Classifier PoC的per-type difficulty gradient是theoretically informative——\n      它mirror了human ambiguity detection difficulty。CP的near-perfect detection\n      vs incompleteness的near-chance performance支持Disambiguation Channel Framework：\n      types with explicit linguistic markers are detectable; types defined by information absence are not。\n      Best档下这个insight在Discussion section获得一段话。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":